{"seq":23,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T13:30:15.469Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"7b473541ea96861ac234b9f6fc0848ea9329851212fb9138a2e0372aff5e0a92","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Pree, here are the Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers I found:\n\n1. *PD-5302*: #central-random, Hollis, Oct 14. He named it outright as another Marrow Fieldworks ticket, for a follow-up from this week.\n2. *#8841*: #central-random, Tobias, Oct 13. West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. Tobias filed it under \"Tobias's dealer account\" and didn't name the account. I'm counting it as Fieldworks because Moss's note says Fieldworks changed hands on 5 Jan, but please check that with Tobias.\n3. *#4409*: Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (teams/team-central/digests, 2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at Salina North (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, 06:00 flatbed intake).\n4. *#4412*: the same Moss digest. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n\nOn #4409 and #4412: the digest lists them as \"two open support tickets on Pree's dealer account\" right under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff line. It never puts the Fieldworks name on the tickets themselves.\n\nTwo more tickets turned up that belong to Marrow *Agrisupply*, not Fieldworks, so I left them off the list: FR-882 (Moss's 2 Jan digest) and PD-4821 (#central-team, Jun 9). This week's chat in #central-team, #general, #help-it-ops and #inc-tansley-carrier-api has no other Fieldworks tickets."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
